## Step 1 — Read inventory

Parse **[Feature inventory (shipped vs planned)]** and **Roadmap modules (Planning cards only)**. Use **Routes** / **Database** only for extra context when writing **What it does** / **Next step**.

Expand **Roadmap modules** into one ClickUp task each when listed there and not already a dedicated inventory row: Insurance tracking, Scenario simulator, Dependents planning, Estate checklist, Wealth reports (quarterly reports), Documents vault, Risk profiling, Account syncing, Retirement planning studio (Partial), AI insights (Planned — also inventory Home row).

Split broad inventory lines into product tasks where ClickUp already uses separate titles (e.g. Home metrics → Client home dashboard, Net worth summary, Monthly spending view; proposals → Advisor proposal flow + Proposal review page).

## Step 2 — Build ClickUp task payloads

For each product row, set:

| ClickUp field | Source |
|---------------|--------|
| **Task name** | Product name from mapping table below |
| **Status** (native) | See status mapping |
| **Description** | Structured plain text (see format below) |
| **Area** (custom) | From mapping defaults |
| **User Type** (custom) | From mapping defaults |
| **Priority** (custom) | Default from mapping; if task exists, **keep** current Priority unless status flipped to Partial/Planned on a formerly Done item → bump toward High |
| **Next step** (custom) | Short action from inventory gap; if task exists and inventory unchanged, **keep** existing Next step |
| **Tags** | Comma-separated tags from mapping when creating; on update, add missing tags only (do not remove tags unless user asks) |

**Description format** (plain text, pipe-separated sections):

```
What it does: <one sentence> | Examples: <1–2 examples> | Current app behaviour: <shipped/partial/planned fact> | Gaps and next steps: <gap from inventory Notes>
```

No file paths or backticks in stakeholder copy.

| `PROJECT_CONTEXT` status | ClickUp **status** (native) |
|--------------------------|----------------------------|
| **Shipped** | `DONE` — code implemented per inventory; automation may set this only |
| **Partial** | `NOT STARTED` |
| **Planned** | `OPEN` |
| **Not in repo** | `OPEN` |

### Native statuses — do not automate

These are **manual only** (never set or clear via sync; leave unchanged when updating descriptions or custom fields):

| Status | Who moves it |
|--------|----------------|
| `READY TO TEST` | You — after you want something in test |
| `TO BE DISCUSSED` | Team — discussion queue |
| `TESTED` | QA sign-off (formerly `TESTED BY DARREN`) |

**Before any status update:** read the task’s current native status. If it is one of the three above, **omit `status`** from `clickup_update_task` (update description / custom fields only). Do not downgrade `TESTED`, `READY TO TEST`, or `TO BE DISCUSSED` without explicit user instruction.

`DONE` means **repo implementation recognized** in `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` (inventory **Shipped**), not “released to users” or “QA complete”. Downstream QA (`READY TO TEST` → `TESTED` → `CLOSED`) stays manual.

If a status string is rejected by the API, run `clickup_filter_tasks` on this list and use an existing status name from returned tasks before retrying.

**User Type** for scope rows: `Admin` or `Needs confirmation` as in mapping. Others: `Client`, `Advisor`, or `Client; Advisor` (semicolon-separated).

